    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the advice. the thing is, i actually tried to peek through the gaps in the casing yesterday to see if it was just a loose wire or something, and i swear i saw something small and dark dart back into the corner of the box right as the light flickered. it was way too fast to be a rat or a bird. it almost seemed like it was... i don't know, playing a game with the switch?\n\nit's just so weirdly specific and almost feels like it's being done on purpose to be a nuisance. do you think it's possible for these types of electrical systems to just... have these kinds of weird, inexplicable glitches that feel more like a prank than a broken part?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
